==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|bera|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpɛːra/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːra|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|Bera}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bar|báru|borið}}

# {{context|governs the accusative}} to [[carry]], to [[bear]]{{jump|is|carry|s}}
# {{context|governs the accusative|of cows and sheep}} to [[give birth]]{{jump|is|give birth|s}}
# {{context|impersonal|lang=is}} denotes an [[obligation]] or [[duty]] to do something
#: ''Mér '''ber''' að fara í stríð.''
#:: It '''is''' my '''duty''' to go to [[war]].

