==Old English==

===Etymology===
From West Germanic root ''*beran-'', from [[Proto-Indo-European]] root {{proto|title=|Indo-European|bʰer-|brown animal|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old High German ''[[bero]]'' (German ''[[Bär]]''), Middle Dutch ''[[bere]]'' (Dutch ''[[beer#Dutch|beer]]''), Old Norse ''[[ber]]''.  A North Germanic variant, ''*bernu-'', gave Old Norse {{Latinx|[[bjǫrn]]}} (Swedish ''[[björn]]'').  The Proto-Indo-European root is also the source of Slavic ''*brlog'' (Russian {{term|берлога|lang=ru||den}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈberɑ/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
'''bera''' {{m}}

# [[bear]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun|bera|beran|beran|beran|beran|berena|beran|berum}}

====Descendants====
* English: [[bear]]

